  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Federal contract obligations in North Dakota total $636M in FY2026 to date. Award activity includes 2,079 awards with an average award size of $306K. Obligations are down 22.5% year over year. Fiscal-year comparisons show variability: FY21 recorded $780M, FY22 recorded $973M, FY23 recorded $803M, FY24 recorded $980M, FY25 recorded $821M, and FY26 recorded $636M. The Department of Health and Human Services is the largest buying agency with $278M in obligations, followed by the Department of Defense with $167M and the Department of Transportation with $86.1M. NORIDIAN HEALTHCARE SOLUTIONS, LLC is the largest vendor with $258M in obligations, followed by WALSH FEDERAL LLC with $74.4M and PACKET DIGITAL LLC with $36.8M. Direct Health and Medical Insurance Carriers is the largest industry by obligations at $222M, followed by Commercial and Institutional Building Construction at $115M. All figures are contract obligations; current-year totals are partial (fiscal year to date).",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "What trends stand out in FY2026 to date?",
        "body": "Fiscal-year obligations for North Dakota show swings historically and a decline into FY26: FY21 was $780M, FY22 was $973M, FY23 was $803M, FY24 was $980M, FY25 was $821M, and FY26 is $636M. Obligations are down 22.5% year over year, and average award size in FY26 is $306K across 2,079 awards."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which industries and vendors dominate federal contracting in North Dakota?",
        "body": "Direct Health and Medical Insurance Carriers leads industries with $222M in obligations, and Commercial and Institutional Building Construction follows with $115M. NORIDIAN HEALTHCARE SOLUTIONS, LLC leads vendors with $258M, WALSH FEDERAL LLC follows with $74.4M, and PACKET DIGITAL LLC follows with $36.8M."
      }
    ]
  },
